{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:06:26Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 58, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\tThe frontend `clearCompleted()` at `frontend/src/api.js:26` matches the new `DELETE /api/tasks/completed` route and expects a JSON body (`{count: int}`), which the new `ClearResult` response provides correctly.\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\t\n5\tThe backend half of Taiga #9 was genuinely missing (confirmed by the review), and an earlier partial attempt had left some inconsistent/duplicated state across files, which I found and cleaned up during implementation. Final state:\n6\t\n7\t- **`backend/app/models.py`** \u2014 added `ClearResult(BaseModel)` with a single `count: int` field.\n8\t- **`backend/app/store.py:94-100`** \u2014 added `TaskStore.clear_completed() -> int`, matching the shape of `delete()`: removes all done tasks, calls `self._save()` once only if anything changed, returns the count removed.\n9\t- **`backend/app/main.py:56-58`** \u2014 added `DELETE /api/tasks/completed` \u2192 `ClearResult`, declared **above** `@app.delete(\"/api/tasks/{task_id}\")` at what's now line 61, avoiding the route-ordering hazard the spec flagged.\n10\t- **`backend/tests/test_tasks.py`** \u2014 4 new tests: empty store (AC6), no-completed-tasks no-op (AC1), mixed removal with open tasks preserved (AC2), no `done: true` tasks remain afterward (AC3).\n11\t- **`backend/tests/test_persistence.py:87-101`** \u2014 `test_cleared_completed_tasks_do_not_reappear_after_restart` already existed from the earlier attempt and correctly covers AC5; left as-is.\n12\t\n13\tAC4 (filter-independence) has no backend dimension \u2014 the store has no concept of a filter, so `clear_completed()` is inherently store-wide.\n14\t\n15\tVerified: full backend suite passes (35/35, `python3 -m pytest -q`), including the 4 new tests run in isolation. Frontend `clearCompleted()` in `api.js:26` already matches this contract exactly, so no frontend changes were needed.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Ck6J5KMBNY56cE1vAD33BB", "session_id": "70bd593b-f46c-4d0b-b840-0d4bce54ac33"}}
