{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:06:44Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 82, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "commit 5a1027e59814fe540aa7cf26fdde75ca0bb33eec\nAuthor: test-project <dev@test-project.local>\nDate:   Mon Aug 17 08:53:01 2026 +0000\n\n    Allow the pipeline roles to work without an approval prompt\n    \n    A headless agent turn cannot answer an interactive approval prompt, so round 1\n    produced nothing: the story stage could not write docs/spec.md, and every\n    downstream role correctly refused to invent what was missing.\n    \n    This is a scoped allowlist rather than a blanket bypass. Writes are limited to\n    the source, test and docs trees; the commands allowed are the ones this\n    project actually documents for building and testing. Pushing, resetting,\n    sudo, host tooling and .git writes are explicitly denied, so the blast radius\n    of an agent that goes wrong stays inside the working tree and stays\n    recoverable.\n    \n    Verified against a real headless dispatch: the agent wrote a file and ran the\n    backend suite (8 passed) with no prompt.\n\n .claude/settings.json | 53 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 53 insertions(+)\n---\ncommit 5a1027e59814fe540aa7cf26fdde75ca0bb33eec\nAuthor: test-project <dev@test-project.local>\nDate:   Mon Aug 17 08:53:01 2026 +0000\n\n    Allow the pipeline roles to work without an approval prompt\n    \n    A headless agent turn cannot answer an interactive approval prompt, so round 1\n    produced nothing: the story stage could not write docs/spec.md, and every\n    downstream role correctly refused to invent what was missing.\n    \n    This is a scoped allowlist rather than a blanket bypass. Writes are limited to\n    the source, test and docs trees; the commands allowed are the ones this\n    project actually documents for building and testing. Pushing, resetting,\n    sudo, host tooling and .git writes are explicitly denied, so the blast radius\n    of an agent that goes wrong stays inside the working tree and stays\n    recoverable.\n    \n    Verified against a real headless dispatch: the agent wrote a file and ran the\n    backend suite (8 passed) with no prompt.\n\ndiff --git a/.claude/settings.json b/.claude/settings.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..c2913a5\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/.claude/settings.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@\n+{\n+  \"permissions\": {\n+    \"allow\": [\n+      \"Read\",\n+      \"Glob\",\n+      \"Grep\",\n+      \"Write(./backend/**)\",\n+      \"Write(./frontend/src/**)\",\n+      \"Write(./e2e/**)\",\n+      \"Write(./docs/**)\",\n+      \"Edit(./backend/**)\",\n+      \"Edit(./frontend/src/**)\",\n+      \"Edit(./e2e/**)\",\n+      \"Edit(./docs/**)\",\n+      \"Edit(./CLAUDE.md)\",\n+      \"Bash(python3 -m pytest*)\",\n+      \"Bash(python3 -m playwright*)\",\n+      \"Bash(npm run build*)\",\n+      \"Bash(npm run dev*)\",\n+      \"Bash(npm test*)\",\n+      \"Bash(npm ci*)\",\n+      \"Bash(npm install*)\",\n+      \"Bash(git status*)\",\n+      \"Bash(git diff*)\",\n+      \"Bash(git log*)\",\n+      \"Bash(git show*)\",\n+      \"Bash(git branch*)\",\n+      \"Bash(git add*)\",\n+      \"Bash(git rev-parse*)\",\n+      \"Bash(ls*)\",\n+      \"Bash(cat*)\",\n+      \"Bash(head*)\",\n+      \"Bash(tail*)\",\n+      \"Bash(grep*)\",\n+      \"Bash(rg*)\",\n+      \"Bash(find*)\",\n+      \"Bash(wc*)\",\n+      \"Bash(curl http://127.0.0.1:*)\",\n+      \"Bash(curl http://localhost:*)\"\n+    ],\n+    \"deny\": [\n+      \"Bash(rm -rf*)\",\n+      \"Bash(git push*)\",\n+      \"Bash(git reset --hard*)\",\n+      \"Bash(git clean*)\",\n+      \"Bash(sudo*)\",\n+      \"Bash(pct*)\",\n+      \"Bash(systemctl*)\",\n+      \"Write(./.git/**)\",\n+      \"Read(./**/.env)\"\n+    ]\n+  }\n+}", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_011odCwex1QHrbWAxFfqp7N3", "session_id": "70bd593b-f46c-4d0b-b840-0d4bce54ac33"}}
