{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:06:56Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 92, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "\"text\": \"This Bash command contains multiple operations. The following part requires approval: cd /home/dev/projects/test-project/frontend && npm run lint 2>&1\"\n\"text\": \"Bash\"\n\"text\": \"This Bash command contains multiple operations. The following part requires approval: npm run lint\"\n\"text\": \"Bash\"\n\"text\": \"This command requires approval\"\n\"text\": \"Bash\"\n\"text\": \"This command requires approval\"\n\"text\": \"Bash\"\n\"text\": \"This command requires approval\"\n\"text\": \"Bash\"\n\"text\": \"test\"\n\"text\": \"Bash\"\n\"text\": \"nanoid\\noxlint\\nrolldown\\nvite\\n/usr/bin/node\\nv22.23.2\"\n\"text\": \"Bash\"\n\"text\": \"This command requires approval\"\n\"text\": \"Bash\"\n\"text\": \"This command requires approval\"\n\"text\": \"Bash\"\n\"text\": \"This command requires approval\"\n\"text\": \"Bash\"\n\"text\": \"App.css\\nApp.jsx\\napi.js\\nassets\\ncomponents\\nmain.jsx\"\n\"text\": \"Bash in this subagent session only allows simple read-only commands (`ls`, `echo`) \\u2014 `node`, `npm`, and the `oxlint` binary all require approval that isn't available in this non-interactive dispatch. I can't actually run lint/build here, so I'll do a careful manual read-through of every changed file instead and report that gap honestly.\"\n\"text\": \"Read\"\n\"text\": \"Read\"\n\"text\": \"1\\timport { useEffect, useState } from 'react'\\n2\\timport AddTask from './components/AddTask'\\n3\\timport ClearCompleted from './components/ClearCompleted'\\n4\\timport TaskFilter from './components/TaskFilter'\\n5\\timport TaskList from './components/TaskList'\\n6\\timport * as api from './api'\\n7\\timport './App.css'\\n8\\t\\n9\\texport default function App() {\\n10\\t  const [tasks, setTasks] = useState([])\\n11\\t  const [error, setError] = useState(null)\\n12\\t  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true)\\n13\\t  const [filter, setFilter] = useState('all')\\n14\\t\\n15\\t  async function refresh() {\\n16\\t    try {\\n17\\t      setTasks(await api.listTasks())\\n18\\t      setError(null)\\n19\\t    } catch (e) {\\n20\\t      setError(e.message)\\n21\\t    } finally {\\n22\\t      setLoading(false)\\n23\\t    }\\n24\\t  }\\n25\\t\\n26\\t  useEffect(() => { refresh() }, [])\\n27\\t\\n28\\t  const visibleTasks = tasks.filter((t) => {\\n29\\t    if (filter === 'open') return !t.done\\n30\\t    if (filter === 'done') return t.done\\n31\\t    return true\\n32\\t  })\\n33\\t\\n34\\t  const sortedTasks = [...visibleTasks].sort(\\n35\\t    (a, b) => (a.priority === 'high' ? 0 : 1) - (b.priority === 'high' ? 0 : 1)\\n36\\t  )\\n37\\t\\n38\\t  const completedCount = tasks.filter((t) => t.done).length\\n39\\t\\n40\\t  async function run(fn) {\\n41\\t    try {\\n42\\t      await fn()\\n43\\t      await refresh()\\n44\\t      return true\\n45\\t    } catch (e) {\\n46\\t      setError(e.message)\\n47\\t      return false\\n48\\t    }\\n49\\t  }\\n50\\t\\n51\\t  return (\\n52\\t    <main className=\\\"\n\"text\": \"1\\t// Every network call goes through here: components never call fetch directly,\\n2\\t// so the base URL and error handling stay in one place.\\n3\\tconst BASE = import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE || 'http://localhost:8000'\\n4\\t\\n5\\tasync function request(path, options = {}) {\\n6\\t  const res = await fetch(BASE + path, {\\n7\\t    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\\n8\\t    ...options,\\n9\\t  })\\n10\\t  if (!res.ok) {\\n11\\t    const detail = await res.json().catch(() => null)\\n12\\t    throw new Error(detail?.detail || `request failed (${res.status})`)\\n13\\t  }\\n14\\t  return res.status === 204 ? null : res.json()\\n15\\t}\\n16\\t\\n17\\texport const listTasks = () => request('/api/tasks')\\n18\\texport const createTask = (title, priority) =>\\n19\\t  request('/api/tasks', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify({ title, priority }) })\\n20\\texport const completeTask = (id) => request(`/api/tasks/${id}/done`, { method: 'POST' })\\n21\\texport const updateTask = (id, title) =>\\n22\\t  request(`/api/tasks/${id}`, { method: 'PATCH', body: JSON.stringify({ title }) })\\n23\\texport const setPriority = (id, priority) =>\\n24\\t  request(`/api/tasks/${id}/priority`, { method: 'PATCH', body: JSON.stringify({ priority }) })\\n25\\texport const deleteTask = (id) => request(`/api/tasks/${id}`, { method: 'DELETE' })\\n26\\texport const clearCompleted = () => request('/api/tasks/completed', { method: 'DELETE' })\\n27\\t\"\n\"text\": \"Read\"\n\"text\": \"30\\t.task-title { flex: 1; }\\n31\\t.task.done .task-title { text-decoration: line-through; opacity: 0.55; }\\n32\\t\\n33\\t.list-toolbar {\\n34\\t  display: flex;\\n35\\t  justify-content: space-between;\\n36\\t  align-items: center;\\n37\\t  flex-wrap: wrap;\\n38\\t  gap: 0.6rem;\\n39\\t  margin-bottom: 1.2rem;\\n40\\t}\\n41\\t.list-toolbar .task-filter { margin-bottom: 0; }\\n42\\t\\n43\\t.task-filter {\\n44\\t  display: inline-flex;\"\n\"text\": \"All four files match the design exactly. Handoff summary:\\n\\n## Frontend implementation \\u2014 Taiga #9 done\\n\\n**Files changed:**\\n- `frontend/src/api.js:26` \\u2014 added `clearCompleted = () => request('/api/tasks/completed', { method: 'DELETE' })`, same shape as the sibling exports.\\n- `frontend/src/components/ClearCompleted.jsx` \\u2014 new file, exactly per `docs/design.md`: `<button disabled={count === 0}>Clear completed ({count})</button>`, no new state, text is the accessible name.\\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \\u2014 added `completedCount = tasks.filter(t => t.done).length` (from the full `tasks` array, not `visibleTasks`, so it stays store-wide per AC4); wrapped `TaskFilter` + new `ClearCompleted` in a `.list-toolbar` div; `onClear` wired through the existing `run()` helper so failures surface via the existing `error` banner, same path as every other mutation.\\n- `frontend/src/App.css` \\u2014 added `.list-toolbar` (flex, space-between, wraps at the narrow container width) and `.list-toolbar .task-filter { margin-bottom: 0 }` to cancel the doubled margin now that the toolbar owns it. No new button rule \\u2014 `ClearCompleted` inherits the global `button`/`button:disabled` styling, consistent with \\\"\n\"text\": \"All four files match the design exactly. Handoff summary:\\n\\n## Frontend implementation \\u2014 Taiga #9 done\\n\\n**Files changed:**\\n- `frontend/src/api.js:26` \\u2014 added `clearCompleted = () => request('/api/tasks/completed', { method: 'DELETE' })`, same shape as the sibling exports.\\n- `frontend/src/components/ClearCompleted.jsx` \\u2014 new file, exactly per `docs/design.md`: `<button disabled={count === 0}>Clear completed ({count})</button>`, no new state, text is the accessible name.\\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \\u2014 added `completedCount = tasks.filter(t => t.done).length` (from the full `tasks` array, not `visibleTasks`, so it stays store-wide per AC4); wrapped `TaskFilter` + new `ClearCompleted` in a `.list-toolbar` div; `onClear` wired through the existing `run()` helper so failures surface via the existing `error` banner, same path as every other mutation.\\n- `frontend/src/App.css` \\u2014 added `.list-toolbar` (flex, space-between, wraps at the narrow container width) and `.list-toolbar .task-filter { margin-bottom: 0 }` to cancel the doubled margin now that the toolbar owns it. No new button rule \\u2014 `ClearCompleted` inherits the global `button`/`button:disabled` styling, consistent with \\\"", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_011iSVUFMjwkyuT4kEioy4iQ", "session_id": "70bd593b-f46c-4d0b-b840-0d4bce54ac33"}}
