{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:07:27Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 117, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\tClean tree, no stray artifacts. Review complete.\n2\t\n3\t## Review: Taiga #9 \u2014 Clear all completed tasks at once\n4\t\n5\t**Verified:** full backend suite (35/35 passing, including 4 new tests), frontend `npm run build` clean, route-ordering hazard from the spec correctly avoided (`/api/tasks/completed` declared above `/api/tasks/{task_id}`), all 6 spec ACs traced to passing test coverage or working code, `git status` clean (no stray artifacts).\n6\t\n7\t### Will block\n8\t\n9\tNone.\n10\t\n11\t### Will comment\n12\t\n13\tNone.\n14\t\n15\t### Worth considering\n16\t\n17\t- `backend/app/store.py:94-97` (Leonard Teichmann \u2014 functional style) \u2014 `clear_completed()` builds a list of `done_ids` then deletes them in a loop. A single dict-comprehension rewrite (`self._tasks = {k: v for k, v in self._tasks.items() if not v.done}`) reads more directly as \"keep the non-done tasks\" and avoids the intermediate list, though the current two-step version is correct and no less readable than the existing imperative `delete()` it deliberately mirrors. Not worth a round-trip on its own.\n18\t\n19\tEverything else checks out: `ClearResult` is a minimal, honest response model; `TaskStore.clear_completed()` matches the shape and save-only-on-change discipline of its siblings; the route sits above the ordering hazard the spec flagged; the frontend button is disabled at count 0 (satisfying AC1's \"no API call\" requirement structurally, not just by convention), computes its count from the full `tasks` list rather than the filtered view (AC4), and is wired through the existing `run()` helper so errors surface the same way every other mutation's do; CSS reuses the existing plain-button styling with no new visual language, as the design doc specified. No frontend test scaffolding exists anywhere in this project (no `test` script, no test files, no testing library in `package.json`) \u2014 that's a pre-existing gap, not something this diff should be asked to fix.\n20\t\n21\tVERDICT: approve", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_016g675NV3VhyY5P5bL9XSw3", "session_id": "70bd593b-f46c-4d0b-b840-0d4bce54ac33"}}
