{"ts": "2026-08-17T12:07:30Z", "agent": "claude-edits", "seq": 120, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "1\t## Verification report \u2014 Taiga #9: Clear all completed tasks\n2\t\n3\tThe findings I was handed claim the backend half of this feature is \"entirely missing.\" That does not match the current working tree \u2014 `git diff --stat` shows all the backend files already modified, and every piece described as missing is present and working:\n4\t\n5\t**Backend \u2014 verified by running the actual suite**\n6\t- `backend/app/models.py` \u2014 `ClearResult(BaseModel)` with `count: int`, present.\n7\t- `backend/app/store.py:94-100` \u2014 `TaskStore.clear_completed()` present, mirrors `delete()`'s save-only-on-change discipline.\n8\t- `backend/app/main.py:56-58` \u2014 `DELETE /api/tasks/completed` route present, declared **above** `@app.delete(\"/api/tasks/{task_id}\")` (line 61+), so the route-ordering hazard the spec flagged is genuinely avoided \u2014 confirmed by running the route through `TestClient`, not just reading it (`test_clear_completed_removes_only_done_tasks` asserts `status_code == 200`, which a 422 mis-route would fail).\n9\t- `python3 -m pytest -q` in `backend/`: **35 passed**, including all 4 new tests (`test_clear_completed_on_empty_store_returns_zero` AC6, `test_clear_completed_with_no_completed_tasks_removes_nothing` AC1, `test_clear_completed_removes_only_done_tasks` AC2, `test_clear_completed_leaves_no_done_tasks_in_list` AC3) and the pre-existing `test_cleared_completed_tasks_do_not_reappear_after_restart` (AC5).\n10\t\n11\t**Frontend \u2014 verified by reading the wiring and building**\n12\t- `frontend/src/api.js:26` `clearCompleted()` calls `DELETE /api/tasks/completed`, matching the backend contract exactly.\n13\t- `frontend/src/components/ClearCompleted.jsx` \u2014 button disabled at `count === 0` (AC1, structurally prevents any click from firing).\n14\t- `frontend/src/App.jsx:38,58` \u2014 `completedCount` is derived from the full `tasks` array, not `visibleTasks`, so it's correctly filter-independent (AC4). Wired through the existing `run()` helper so errors surface via the same `error` banner as every other mutation.\n15\t- `npm run build` \u2014 clean, no errors.\n16\t\n17\tAll six spec ACs trace to passing, real test runs or directly-inspected code, not inference. The review that produced the \"changes-requested\" verdict appears to have been evaluating a stale or different state of the tree \u2014 nothing here supports \"clicking the button does nothing but show a 422.\" I'm not making any code changes since there's nothing broken to fix; flagging the discrepancy instead of silently redoing already-correct work.\n18\t\n19\tVERDICT: pass", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Qphw8TM5F6N5qMJMmGq66b", "session_id": "70bd593b-f46c-4d0b-b840-0d4bce54ac33"}}
